</ul><h1>Not A Cat Toy</h1><p>Dear Diary,</p>
<p>The upright thumbed morons, aka humans, who sublet a room within my house have really outdone themselves this time.</p>
<p>I was taking my third mid-afternoon nap, which I absolutely need if I am to have enough energy to fulfill my nightly duty of yowling in the basement for hours on end, when what should I hear but a terrible mechanical ruckus.</p>
<p>Peering about the room, I saw something peculiar: an intruder.</p>
<p>It’s hard to describe, but it appeared like some of the strange vehicles that often drive loudly by, disturbing the squirrels lounging at the side of the road, whom I was attempting to kill with nothing more than my cold stare. They possess an odd shape, these vehicles; their riders are concentrated to the front, while in the back is a negative space like an open box.</p>
<p>This was one of those, only smaller, and with absurdly outsized wheels.</p>
<p>Of course, my instincts kicked in. I am, by nature, a hunter. The upright thumbed morons often commend me when I hunt things that come from outside to make their home within the house I generously share. So I emerged from my slumber, leapt off the laundry basket I’d selected for my repose, and rushed across the floor to give this strange thing a firm swat.</p>
<p>And how was I repaid for this valiant attack?</p>
<p>By being yelled at.</p>
<p>Adding insult to injury, the humans then brought this strange new item outside. You know, where I am not allowed to go. Because I would “run away” and “never come back.” And they proceeded to play with it and celebrate its every move, as it drove over grass, concrete, dirt, and whatnot.</p>
<p>Though they never once looked towards the window from which I observed them, I understood that this was meant to insult me. (How could it not? After all, everything is done or not done with me in mind.) As a result, I will have to retaliate. It’s time to take a clumsy walk across the mantle above the fireplace where all the vases and glass-framed photographs reside.</p>
<p>I’ll fill you in on the outcome next time.</p>
<ul>
<li>Giovani Vincent Alberto Montessi (alias Mittens)</li>
</ul>